e people who  talks about this earlier than Cicero  that the friend is in in a certain way  here he says a kind of image an exemplar  of oneself in other places in this text  a little bit later on he will bring up  the proverb that a friend is another  self and that we we sometimes think of  ourselves as you know two souls or one  soul and two bodies that there's a  connection between us right we talk  about soulmates or things like that and  now this is only possible within a  genuine friendship it's not going to be  something that happens through the  contingencies of just hooking up with  somebody or meeting somebody in a bar  being a classmate or a neighbor although  you know it could blossom and develop  into that if you're both good people but  this he thinks is something that is is  quite valuable for us human beings he  says that whoever looks upon a true  friend looks on this image of himself  and we could think about well why why  does that matter it's not a narcissistic  thing and narcissus of course was the  the youth who died by looking at his  beautiful image in the pool and  forgetting to eat because of that  instead it's a being able to discover  things about yourself you notice that  that later in the book sister will also  say friends have to hold each other to  standards and so that other self could  be the one who says to you man you're  screwing up you need to fix this part of  yourself and then finally one of the  other great advantages of friendship  that Cicero talks about that is very  interesting here is the capacity for  friends to remain present to  to remain you could say active in our  lives even when they are not there and  he gives up several different modalities  of this he says friends though absent  are at hand though in need yet abound  though weak are strong and harder seeing  still though dead are yet alive even the  friends that we've lost are in a certain  way with us why he says the wreck that  we have the tender recollection